// square.lmc - read numbers and output the square of each; stop when 0 is entered
// Input: 5, 12, 0      Output: 25, 144
// n * n is found by adding n to a total, n times. Each square starts again from 0.
// A mailbox holds at most 999, so the biggest square is 31 * 31 = 961: keep inputs to 31 or less.
start   INP
        BRZ finish       // 0 ends the program
        STA n
        STA count        // how many more additions are needed
        LDA zero
        STA total        // start every square from 0
loop    LDA total
        ADD n
        STA total
        LDA count
        SUB one
        STA count
        BRZ show         // n additions done
        BRA loop
show    LDA total
        OUT
        BRA start        // ask for the next number
finish  HLT
n       DAT
count   DAT
total   DAT
one     DAT 1
zero    DAT 0
